    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138-a1">

                <pb facs="0256" n="186" xml:id="pg186"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 29, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to the case of the steamer
                    Oreto, which you are probably aware has been seized at Nassau and is to be tried
                    before the admiralty court of the Bahamas for a breach of the foreign enlistment
                    act, I have the honor to enclose for your information copies of a report and its
                    enclosures from the commissioners of customs with reference to a suggestion I
                    had made to the treasury, that a competent officer should be sent to Nassau to
                    give evidence as to what occurred at Liverpool in the case of that vessel.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>






